    narr:generatedFrom "7197e2e5261482e8ab862a8aa0f16ad8ffe0fb2f" ;
    narr:narration """Xavier's voice here is an expert's, and it moves across four settings. In the weekly thread he [invites the steering group's push before it lands](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_10), argues [pairing two sites through a shared dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), and [flags the thinness of his own evidence](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_21). He sets [a replica-only rule during cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_26), grounded in [a past outage under load](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_24) and priced against [a replica-lag range](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_28); a second thread runs from [an open question on reference-data ownership](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_34) to [a vendor-stays-system-of-record position](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36) argued via [drift between sites](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_38). A week later he [ranks competing arguments for the same rule](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_15), offers [a learning-curve rationale](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_19), and [names a shared unstated assumption](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25); he also [endorses a shortened window while pricing its cost](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_13) and [puts its tightness on the record](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_15). A later review-comment thread re-voices that same endorsement and its cost, [agreeing while naming the slack it removes](narr:Expr_20260928_1_ReviewCommentTinaTeammemberB4B484EaE94D4912B80BD_h8c260252a0a9_5) and [repeating the thin-evidence caveat](narr:Expr_20260928_1_ReviewCommentTinaTeammemberB4B484EaE94D4912B80BD_h8c260252a0a9_17). Newest, a legacy-archive thread: he [rejects keeping the old platform alive](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7), argues [extracting closed history into a self-describing archive](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9), insists [the meaning is what rots](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13), names [why the argument never gets done](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15), and [commits to a deadline](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_28).""" ;
    narr:reaction """The mainline holds — the earlier narration's arc from cutover rules to the legacy-archive commitment still stands. What's new is a review-comment thread that [re-voices the shortened-window endorsement and its cost](narr:Expr_20260928_1_ReviewCommentTinaTeammemberB4B484EaE94D4912B80BD_h8c260252a0a9_5), so the tight-not-safe caveat now reads as a repeated, dated position rather than a one-off remark — the tension in the old narration sharpened rather than resolved.""" ;
